# CVE-2024-23342 (GHSA-wj6h-64fc-37mp / PYSEC-2026-1325)
# Minerva timing attack on the P-256 curve in python-ecdsa.
#
# python-ecdsa is pulled in transitively by python-jose. Upstream
# (tlsfuzzer/python-ecdsa) states side-channel attacks are out of scope
# for the project and there is NO planned fix, so no version bump can
# clear this finding.
#
# Not reachable in this application: docker-compose.yml sets
# JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256 and no ES256 keypair is configured, so python-jose
# never touches the ecdsa code path (ecdsa is only used for the ES*
# algorithms). The advisory also states signature VERIFICATION is
# unaffected; only nonce-leaking signing would be exposed.
#
# Accepted risk. Revisit when python-jose drops the ecdsa dependency or
# when ES256 signing is ever enabled.
CVE-2024-23342